---
import { getCollection, getEntry } from "astro:content";
import CopyButton from "./CopyButton.astro";
import { Code } from "astro:components";

const commands = (await getEntry("commands", "main"))!.data;

const tabs = (await getCollection("clients"))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .map((c) => ({
    id: c.id,
    label: c.data.label,
    lang: c.data.lang,
    hint: c.data.hint,
    code: c.data.useStandardJson ? commands.standardJson : (c.data.code ?? commands.claudeMcpAdd),
  }));

const mcpTools = (await getCollection("mcpTools"))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .map((t) => [t.data.name, t.data.desc] as const);
---
<section id="mcp" class="relative overflow-hidden bg-ink-950 py-20 sm:py-28 text-ink-100">
  <span id="agents" class="sr-only"></span>
  <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-400">Optional MCP</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-balance text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
        The folders are real. MCP is extra.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-balance text-lg text-ink-300">
        Anything that can <code class="font-mono text-base text-ink-100">cd</code> already works. A second binary, <code class="font-mono text-base text-ink-100">sync-worktrees-mcp</code>, speaks MCP over stdio if a client wants to list, create, or sync worktrees without guessing paths.
      </p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 px-3 py-1 text-xs text-ink-400">
        Works from any managed worktree; <code class="font-mono">sync</code> and <code class="font-mono">initialize</code> also need your config, found from a parent directory or loaded at runtime.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/70 p-1.5 shadow-2xl" data-tabs>
      <div role="tablist" aria-label="MCP setup per AI tool" class="flex flex-wrap gap-1 rounded-xl bg-ink-950/60 p-1">
        {tabs.map((t, i) => (
          <button
            type="button"
            role="tab"
            id={`mcp-tab-${t.id}`}
            data-tab={t.id}
            aria-controls={`mcp-panel-${t.id}`}
            aria-selected={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"}
            tabindex={i === 0 ? 0 : -1}
            class="tab-button rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-ink-300 transition hover:text-white"
          >
            {t.label}
          </button>
        ))}
      </div>

      {tabs.map((t, i) => (
        <div
          role="tabpanel"
          id={`mcp-panel-${t.id}`}
          data-panel={t.id}
          aria-labelledby={`mcp-tab-${t.id}`}
          tabindex="0"
          hidden={i === 0 ? undefined : true}
          class="tab-panel p-4 sm:p-5"
        >
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-400">{t.hint}</p>
            <CopyButton value={t.code} class="bg-ink-800 text-ink-200 hover:bg-ink-700" />
          </div>
          <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-ink-800 bg-ink-950/80">
            <Code code={t.code} lang={t.lang as any} theme="github-dark-default" wrap />
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr]">
      <div>
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-300">
          Example workflow
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Open <code class="font-mono text-xl text-ink-100">backend</code>'s <code class="font-mono text-xl text-ink-100">release/next</code> worktree while you sit in <code class="font-mono text-xl text-ink-100">frontend/main</code>.
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-ink-300">
          Both are directories. An editor, a shell, or an MCP client can use them. If you do wire up MCP, the tools look like this:
        </p>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-ink-300">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-ink-400">1</span><span><code class="font-mono text-ink-100">detect_context</code>: config, repos, worktrees, and what works from here</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-ink-400">2</span><span><code class="font-mono text-ink-100">list_worktrees</code>: status across repos</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-ink-400">3</span><span><code class="font-mono text-ink-100">get_worktree_status</code>: one branch in detail</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-ink-400">4</span><span><code class="font-mono text-ink-100">create_worktree</code>: branch a fix</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-ink-400">5</span><span><code class="font-mono text-ink-100">sync</code>: fetch, create, prune, update</span></li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold text-white">What an agent cannot do through it</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-ink-300">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-ink-500">–</span><span>Delete, trash, restore or purge anything directly. The only removal paths are <code class="font-mono text-ink-100">sync</code>'s own, with the same gates and destinations as the CLI. <code class="font-mono text-ink-100">sync</code> is flagged destructive, so clients can prompt.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-ink-500">–</span><span>Move an existing remote branch. Pushes are create-only.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-ink-500">–</span><span>Overwrite an existing directory.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-ink-500">–</span><span>Create a branch your filters would prune again, unless it passes <code class="font-mono text-ink-100">force: true</code>.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-400">
          Setup for every client, what the server sees from where it is launched, every tool, safety and a parallel-agents recipe:
          <a href="https://github.com/yordan-kanchelov/sync-worktrees/blob/main/docs/mcp.md" class="text-ink-200 underline decoration-ink-600 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">docs/mcp.md</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900/40 p-5">
        <ul class="divide-y divide-ink-800">
          {mcpTools.map(([name, desc]) => (
            <li class="flex flex-col gap-1 py-3 first:pt-0 last:pb-0 sm:flex-row sm:gap-4">
              <code class="shrink-0 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-accent-300 sm:w-44">{name}</code>
              <span class="text-sm text-ink-300">{desc}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
